      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Building your resume is a time consuming process, so allot enough time for it.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Try to tailor your resume to the role you are applying for.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "All resumes are screened by an ATS (Applicant Tracking System), so you can check your score on websites like “ResumeWorded”.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "They should be 1 page resumes as that’s what is expected from freshers.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Make single column resumes in Latex format.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Try to include all relevant coursework / competition / projects / internships in your resume.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Having 1-2 good finance projects on your resume helps.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Participate in case study competitions.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Do some finance certifications and add them onto your resume.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "You can make minor changes to your resume that you are taking for your interviews.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "try to segregate the sections into time slots so you can attempt as much as possible.",
          "category": "OA preparation",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "don’t lose heart in the process and be prepared.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Ensure you contribute at least 3–4 meaningful qualitative points.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Try to work as a team, acknowledge others points and add on to it.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Make sure you speak for 45 sec - 60 sec per point so the moderator takes note of you.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "If you are not able to answer anything don’t panic makes sure you tell the thought process and approach for it.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "If you make a mistake or there is some misunderstanding in what you were supposed to answer DO NOT PANIC, —your interview isn’t over. One or two mistakes are acceptable so keep your head down and focus on answering the rest of the questions properly.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Once the GD is done you might receive the order of interview, but always be ready there can be changes in last minute and you can be called anytime",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "Make sure you are thorough with all the formulas.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Everything happens simultaneously and can be chaotic, so be relaxed, focused and calm.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "The core essence of the process is not about how much you know but whatever you do, how well-versed you are in it. So focus on learning things deeply rather than trying to do a lot of things.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "During interviews, always maintain proper posture, have a smile on your face, do not panic even if you are unable to answer and at least let the interviewer know what approach you’re thinking about.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "The entire placement cycle is very hectic and stressful but it is important to stay in the present and study without worrying about external factors like market situation, recession, etc. Believe me, it never goes to waste. If you have prepared honestly, you will get opportunities.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 3
        }
